From: substrate
Subject: fb: upgrade fbBlt NULL guard to a low-memory guard

Patch 0013 added an `if (!srcLine || !dstLine)` early-return so a
pixmap with NULL backing storage stops fbBlt instead of segfaulting
on the first deref.  In practice the bad pointers aren't always
exactly zero -- a NULL backing that gets walked one row down through
fbBlt's inner loop lands at dstLine + dstStride, which for a 1024-px
wide 32 bpp scanline is exactly 0x1000.  The plain NULL test misses
this and the X server still crashes with addr=0x00001000 inside the
fbBlt inlined-byte-copy loop (e.g. InitRootWindow -> MapWindow ->
miPaintWindow -> fbOddTile -> fbBlt + 0x4B1 when -retro paints the
stipple tile and a tile pixmap has bogus backing).

Reject pointers below 0x10000 -- substrate pixmap backings come from
malloc and live well above 64 KiB; the framebuffer mmap lives much
higher.  Anything in low memory is junk.

--- a/fb/fbblt.c
+++ b/fb/fbblt.c
@@ -62,13 +62,19 @@
      * isn't in our (minimal) font path — used to crash this function
      * with a NULL deref the moment a client tried to draw with it.
      * Log once and bail instead. */
-    if (!srcLine || !dstLine) {
+    /* Reject NULL AND obviously-junk low-memory pointers (e.g.
+     * dstLine == 0x1000 after some upstream pointer arithmetic on a
+     * NULL backing).  Substrate pixmap backings come from malloc
+     * (well above 64 KiB) and the framebuffer mmap lives much higher,
+     * so anything below 64 KiB is junk -- skip the blit rather than
+     * crash the server walking into low memory. */
+    if ((uintptr_t)srcLine < 0x10000u || (uintptr_t)dstLine < 0x10000u) {
         static int warned = 0;
         if (!warned) {
             warned = 1;
-            ErrorF("fbBlt: NULL %s drawable (src=%p dst=%p w=%d h=%d bpp=%d) "
-                   "— likely a font/pixmap with no bits; skipping.\n",
-                   !srcLine ? "src" : "dst",
+            ErrorF("fbBlt: bogus %s drawable (src=%p dst=%p w=%d h=%d bpp=%d) "
+                   "-- likely missing pixmap bits; skipping.\n",
+                   (uintptr_t)srcLine < 0x10000u ? "src" : "dst",
                    (void *)srcLine, (void *)dstLine, width, height, bpp);
         }
         return;
